cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'iad: C code for Forward and Inverse Radiative Transport using the Adding-Doubling method'
message: 'If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article below.'
type: software

authors:
  - given-names: Scott
    family-names: Prahl
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1468-6851'

version: 4.0.0
date-released: '2026-07-29'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/scottprahl/iad'
url: 'https://omlc.org/software/iad/'

abstract: >-
  iad determines the intrinsic optical properties of flat, layered, scattering
  and absorbing samples from measurements of total reflection and transmission.
  It inverts the adding-doubling solution of the radiative transport equation,
  accounting for Fresnel boundaries, integrating-sphere effects, and light lost
  out the sides of the sample.  The companion program ad performs the forward
  adding-doubling calculation.

keywords:
  - radiative transport
  - adding-doubling
  - inverse adding-doubling
  - integrating sphere
  - optical properties
  - tissue optics

